        </p>

        <p>
            Students can explore training options that match their current
            knowledge and professional goals. Building a strong technical
            foundation, completing hands-on exercises, and preparing for
            relevant entry-level certifications can support career preparation.
        </p>

        <p>
            Before choosing a course, review the syllabus, practical lab
            facilities, duration, fees, and career support available.
            Select a learning path that matches the role you want to pursue.
        </p>

        <h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>1. Which job is best after BCA in Cloud Computing and Cyber Security?</h3>
            <p>
                Cloud Support Engineer, Technical Support Engineer, Network
                Administrator, and SOC Analyst are potential options. The
                best role depends on your interests, skills, and practical
                experience.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>2. Can a BCA graduate start a career in cyber security?</h3>
            <p>
                Yes. A BCA graduate can prepare for entry-level security
                opportunities by learning networking, operating systems,
                security fundamentals, and monitoring tools. Employers may
                have additional education or experience requirements.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>3. Is cloud computing a good career option after BCA?</h3>
            <p>
                Cloud computing can offer opportunities in cloud support,
                administration, and infrastructure operations. Practical
                skills and relevant experience can help strengthen your profile.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>4. Which certifications should I consider after BCA?</h3>
            <p>
                Depending on your chosen career path, you can explore
                entry-level networking, cloud, Linux, or cyber security
                certifications. Check the latest exam syllabus, eligibility,
                and fees before registering.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>5. How can I gain practical IT experience?</h3>
            <p>
                Practise with virtual machines, build networking labs,
                complete cloud projects, document troubleshooting exercises,
                and maintain a portfolio of your work.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>6. Do I need coding skills for cloud computing and cyber security?</h3>
            <p>
                Basic scripting can be useful in both fields. Python, Bash,
                or PowerShell can help automate tasks, analyse information,
                and manage systems. The required level depends on the role.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="gst-faq">
            <h3>7. Can I start in IT support and move into cloud or cyber security?</h3>
            <p>
                Yes. IT support can provide experience with operating systems,
                networking, troubleshooting, and user administration. You can
                then build specialized skills and apply for suitable roles.
            </p>
        </section>

        <h2>Final Thoughts</h2>

        <p>
            A BCA in Cloud Computing and Cyber Security can provide a
            foundation for multiple careers in the IT industry. Whether
            you are interested in cloud support, cyber security, networking,
            system administration, or DevOps, each path requires continuous
            learning and practical experience.
        </p>

        <p>
            Identify your interests, learn the essential technologies,
            practise through projects, and prepare for the requirements
            of your target role. With consistent effort, you can work
            towards building a career in the technology sector.
        </p>

